  - **Reading.** The registered verdict word is "undetermined (truth ill-posed)": under the LN target the tanh embedding rank is still growing at T in most runs (settled 11–19%), and it moves with a 1e-3 perturbation of W2(0). Taken alone, every subset fails the tolerance, with no inputs-only row inside on any of them. On held-out runs the premise failure is confirmed: W1 leaves its decay path at once (R4-a). So is how the criterion fails: `n2_decay` under-counts on tanh (R4-b), and the tanh rank grows after the early check (R4-c). The conditional measured row "does not" account for the rank, so there is no localisation beyond the departure. In the plan's terms, rung 4 does not give a validated LN criterion in the MLP encoder. The registered word is "undetermined", not "fail", and the paper should say both: why (truth ill-posed) and how large the miss is against the truth's ambiguity (post hoc bracket, tanh).
